      "rank": 5,
      "ballot_id": "B001",
      "proposed_laureates": ["Immanuel Bloch", "Juan Ignacio Cirac", "Peter Zoller"],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Ultracold atoms in optical lattices created a controllable platform for studying quantum many-body physics and have made complex models experimentally accessible.",
        "attribution": "Bloch represents decisive experimental realization, while Cirac and Zoller made foundational theoretical contributions to quantum simulation; the proposed laureates span those complementary roles.",
        "maturity": "The platform has produced sustained results over many years and remains active, with its full scientific reach still expanding.",
        "uncertainties": ["The field has many major contributors, and the strongest case for a prize depends on defining the specific foundational achievement."]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 6,
      "ballot_id": "B015",
