      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The prediction and observation of kilonovae linked neutron-star mergers to heavy-element production and helped establish multimessenger astronomy as a powerful way to study the Universe.",
        "attribution": "Metzger and Kasen contributed to the theoretical interpretation, while Tanvir represents observational discovery; the full chain includes many others.",
        "maturity": "The 2017 event provided strong confirmation, but the population, detailed physics, and relative contribution to element production remain active research questions.",
